      "id": "b-20-observability-model-the-current-extraction-s-24",
      "flavour": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The current extraction still carries "
        },
        {
          "insert": "appSessionId",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " because Spectre has existing rows and routes keyed by app sessions. That is acceptable as a generic host-app correlation field. New kernel read paths should resolve from containers first and only fall back to app-session identity for compatibility."
